          "worked": "Replace $x$ by $\\frac{x}{h}$ and $y$ by $\\frac{y}{k}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^3}{h^3}+\\frac{xy^2}{hk^2}+\\frac{y^3}{k^3}&=1\\\\\\frac{8x^3}{h^3}+\\frac{8xy^2}{hk^2}+\\frac{8y^3}{k^3}&=8\\end{align*}$$\n\nMatching the coefficients of $y^3$ and $x^3$ gives\n\n$$\\begin{align*}k^3&=8\\\\k&=2\\\\h^3&=\\frac{8}{27}\\\\h&=\\frac{2}{3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe mixed-term coefficient also agrees:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{8}{hk^2}&=\\frac{8}{(2/3)\\times 2^2}\\\\\\frac{8}{hk^2}&=3\\end{align*}$$",
